  "bounds": "PROTOCOL 4c, facts range cartridge. Forms: R is p ÷ a = ? (answer the quotient), C is p ÷ ? = b (answer the divisor), S is ? ÷ a = b (answer the dividend); p = a × b, the times table read backwards, never ÷ 0, no 0 ÷ ? = 0. Divisors and quotients 0-12. T1 R: easy rows 0, 1, 2, 5, 10 and 11 × a digit, at least 8 with an 11 or 12. T2 R: 12 with 3, 4, 9 (at least 6), pairs of 3, 4, 9 (at least 6), pairs touching 3, 4, 9 from the core. T3 R: 11-12 facts with 6, 7, 8 or 11 × 11, 11 × 12, 12 × 12 (at least 8), pairs of 6, 7, 8 (at least 6). T4 C: core facts with an 11 or 12 (at least 6), core pairs of 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9 (at least 8), a, b 2-12. T5 S: core facts 3-12 with an 11 or 12 (at least 6), any core fact 3-12 (at least 6), plus C (4 with an 11 or 12). Wrong choices: distinct non-negative integers up to 999, at least 2 near and at most 1 far. R: near within 2 of the quotient (GROUP_OFF q+-1, +-2), far SUBTRACTED p-a, MULTIPLIED p×a, TENS_SLIP q+-10. C: near within 2 of the divisor (MISSING_ONE_OFF a+-1, ARITH +-2), far MISSING_SUBTRACTED p-b, MISSING_MULTIPLIED p×b. S: near within the larger factor of the dividend (START_GROUP_OFF p+-a, START_ADDED a+b, START_TENS p+-10 when a factor is 11 or more, with a twin ones digit when p is 20 or more). The answer's rank among the four values is spread 15-35% per tier.",
