  "items_per_tier": 24,
  "bounds": "Mixed facts (PROTOCOL 4c, briefs/facts2): the whole run inside + and − to 10 and × and ÷ with factors to 5, easy to hard by tier. Each tier is 6 items from each of facts-add-10, facts-sub-10, facts-mul-5, facts-div-5 at the same tier: the same pools, forms, distractors, explanations and student text, every part's floor n scaled to ceil(n / 4), at most 2 zero-factor multiplication prompts a tier; 24 items per tier, prompts unique per tier, operations interleaved. Misconception keys carry their operation (ADD_, SUB_, MUL_, DIV_). Answer rank among the 4 values 15-35% each over the whole tier. [ADD] Facts bounds (PROTOCOL 4c, briefs/facts2): the whole run inside sums 1 to 10, easy to hard by tier. Prompt forms: R 'a + b = ?' (answer s), C 'a + ? = s' (answer b), S '? + b = s' (answer a); every number a non-negative integer. T1 R, a or b <= 2 (0 allowed). T2 R, a, b >= 2. T3 R with a, b >= 3 (>= 8) plus C and S on the ten pairs a + (10 - a) (>= 4 each). T4 C, a, b >= 1. T5 S (>= 12) and C, a, b >= 2 and sums 5 to 10. Prompts unique per tier, 24 per tier. Wrong choices: distinct non-negative integers <= 999, >= 2 near the answer (+-1, +-2, +-10), at most 1 far; answer rank among the 4 values 15-35% each per tier; answers >= 20 always have a wrong choice sharing the ones digit (+-10); the answer is never the only value of its parity. [SUB] Sums within 10: s − a = b read as a + b = s backwards (pools.py), items are s − a = ?, s − ? = b, ? − a = b. T1 R, a or b at most 2 (s − 0 included); T2 R, a and b at least 2; T3 R with a and b at least 3 (at least 8) plus the make-ten facts as s − ? = b and ? − a = b (at least 4 each); T4 s − ? = b, a and b at least 1; T5 ? − a = b (at least 12) and s − ? = b with a and b at least 2 and s 5-10. Wrong choices: distinct non-negative integers, at least two within 1 or 2 of the answer, at most one far; no tens slips and no values 10 away within 10; modelled misconceptions first, ARITH only to fill; each answer rank holds the answer in 15-35% of a tier. [MUL] Factors 0 to 5. Forms: R a × b = ?, C a × ? = p, S ? × b = p (a missing factor is never 0). T1 R: a fact with a 0, 1, 2 or 5 (32 prompts); T2 R: both factors 1-5 (25); T3 R: both 2-5 (at least 12 items) and C with 2 or 5 as the first factor, factors 1-5 (at least 8; 26 prompts in all); T4 C: factors 1-5 (25); T5 S: both 2-5 (at least 12 items) and C: both 2-5 (32 prompts in all). At most 6 prompts per tier with a 0 factor. Wrong choices are distinct non-negative whole numbers up to 999. R: at least two within the larger factor of the answer (at least 2), at most one far. C and S: at least two within 2 of the answer, at most one far. Answer ranks (smallest to largest of the four) each hold 15 to 35 percent of a tier. [DIV] PROTOCOL 4c, facts range cartridge. Forms: R is p ÷ a = ? (answer the quotient), C is p ÷ ? = b (answer the divisor), S is ? ÷ a = b (answer the dividend); p = a × b, the times table read backwards, never ÷ 0, no 0 ÷ ? = 0. Divisors and quotients 0-5. T1 R: a or b in {0,1,2,5}. T2 R: a, b 1-5. T3 R: a, b 2-5 (at least 12) plus C with divisor 2 or 5 (at least 8). T4 C: a, b 1-5. T5 S: a, b 2-5 (at least 12) plus C: a, b 2-5. Wrong choices: distinct non-negative integers up to 999, at least 2 near and at most 1 far. R: near within 2 of the quotient (GROUP_OFF q+-1, +-2), far SUBTRACTED p-a, MULTIPLIED p×a, TENS_SLIP q+-10. C: near within 2 of the divisor (MISSING_ONE_OFF a+-1, ARITH +-2), far MISSING_SUBTRACTED p-b, MISSING_MULTIPLIED p×b. S: near within the larger factor of the dividend (START_GROUP_OFF p+-a, START_ADDED a+b, START_TENS p+-10 when a factor is 11 or more, with a twin ones digit when p is 20 or more). The answer's rank among the four values is spread 15-35% per tier.",
